.\" Title: vrc-cat
.\" Author: vrc contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRC-CAT 1 "2025" "vrc" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrc cat \- show VTTY output of a command in a running instance

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrc
\fBcat\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOMMAND\fR] [\fB\-\-plain\fR] [\fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the virtual terminal (VTTY) buffer of a command running inside a vrc instance. By default, the output includes ANSI escape sequences preserving colors, bold, underline, strikethrough, and other formatting exactly as the child process displayed it.

Connects to the target instance's UDS control socket at \fB~/.local/share/vrc/control-{pid}.sock\fR and retrieves the VTTY snapshot.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
OS process ID of the target vrc instance (the vrc process itself, not the child command).

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fICOMMAND\fR
ID of the target command within the instance (omit for the first/only command).

.TP
.BR \-\-plain
Output plain text without ANSI colors or formatting. Strips all escape sequences.

.TP
.BR \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of all commands in the instance and allow the user to select one or more by number (space-separated). Overrides \-c.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Print the VTTY of the only command in an instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc cat 12345\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Print plain text (no colors):
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc cat --plain 12345\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Print a specific command by ID:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc cat 12345 \-c cmd_abc\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Interactively select commands to print:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc cat 12345 \-\-interactive\fR
  1) htop (PID 5678)
  2) vim notes.txt (PID 5679)
Select [space-separated numbers]: 1 2
.fi
.RE

.PP
Pipe plain output to grep:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc cat --plain 12345 | grep "ERROR"\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Pipe colored output to less:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc cat 12345 | less \-R\fR
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Success.

.TP
.B 1
Error (instance not found, connection failed, command not found, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrc (1),
.BR vrc-list (1),
.BR vrc-keys (1),
.BR vrc-spawn-in (1)
